From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:59:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Soloud::mixBus_internal: a ticking voice stops wrapping a
 loop without audio

An inaudible voice that ticks reads its source without mixing it, and
wrapped its loop until the block was full without checking that the wrap
gave any audio, as the mixing path does. A looping sound whose loop point
is at or past its end gives none, so once 3D attenuation made such a
voice inaudible, mix spun forever holding the audio mutex. The wrap now
stops when the source gives no audio, as in the mixing path.
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index 5459915..5ff90c6 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -1930,7 +1930,9 @@ namespace SoLoud
 									while (readcount < SAMPLE_GRANULARITY && voice->seek(voice->mLoopPoint, mSeekScratch.mData, SAMPLE_GRANULARITY * MAX_CHANNELS) == SO_NO_ERROR)
 									{
 										voice->mLoopCount++;
-										readcount += voice->getAudio(voice->mResampleData[0] + readcount, SAMPLE_GRANULARITY - readcount, SAMPLE_GRANULARITY);
+										int inc = voice->getAudio(voice->mResampleData[0] + readcount, SAMPLE_GRANULARITY - readcount, SAMPLE_GRANULARITY);
+										readcount += inc;
+										if (inc == 0) break;
 									}
 								}
 							}
